<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the</p>
<p>opening day of four-day English County Championship cricket</p>
<p>matches on Wednesday:</p>
<p>At The Oval: Somerset 311-5 (R.Harden 81 not out, P.Bowler</p>
<p>63, M.Lathwell 50) v Surrey.</p>
<p>At Hove: Northamptonshire 288-9 (R.Montgomerie 68, D.Capel</p>
<p>57; M.Robinson 5-71) v Sussex.</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex 246 (P.Prichard 65; C.Connor 7-46).</p>
<p>Hampshire 103-7.</p>
<p>At Cardiff: Warwickshire 151 (S.Thomas 4-62). Glamorgan</p>
<p>195-1 (S.James 83, H.Morris 78 not out).</p>
<p>At Canterbury: Kent 251 (M.Ealham 72 not out, S.Marsh 57;</p>
<p>D.Malcolm 6-74). Derbyshire 35-4.</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Lancashire 494-9 (G.Lloyd 102, J.Gallian</p>
<p>78, P.Martin 67 not out, G.Chapple 65 not out, M Watkinson 51) v</p>
<p>Durham.</p>
<p>At Leicester: Gloucestershire 245 (S.Young 59, R.Russell 57;</p>
<p>A.Mullally 5-52). Leicestershire 99-3</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Worcestershire 286-3 (T.Curtis 100 not out,</p>
<p>W.Weston 52) v Nottinghamshire.</p>
</text>
